{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/adopting-common-protocols"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Data-Modeling","generated":true,"title":"Data Modeling","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/choosing-between-structures-and-classes"]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When using custom types to model data in your programs, you may frequently need to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"check whether two values are the same or different, or whether a particular value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is included in a list of values. This capability, as well as the ability to store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values in a set or use them as keys in a dictionary, are governed by two related"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"standard library protocols, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Equatable","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Hashable","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can compare instances of an "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"equatable"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" type by using the equal-to ("},{"code":"==","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not-equal-to ("},{"code":"!=","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") operators."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An instance of a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"hashable"}]},{"type":"text","text":" type can reduce its value mathematically to a single"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"integer, which is used internally by sets and dictionaries to make lookups consistently"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fast."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Many standard library types are both equatable and hashable, including strings, integers,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"floating-point values, Boolean values, and collections of equatable and hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"types. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":" comparison and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method call in the following example"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"depend on strings and integers being equatable:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["if username == \"Arturo\" {","    print(\"Hi, Arturo!\")","}","","let favoriteNumbers = [4, 7, 8, 9]","if favoriteNumbers.contains(todaysDate.day) {","    print(\"It's a good day today!\")","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforming to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" protocols is straightforward and makes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it easier to use your own types in Swift. It’s a good idea for all your custom model"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"types to conform."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Conform-Automatically-to-Equatable-and-Hashable","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Conform Automatically to Equatable and Hashable"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can make many custom types equatable and hashable by simply declaring these protocol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conformances in the same file as the type’s original declaration. Add "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" to the list of adopted protocols when declaring the type, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compiler automatically fills in the requirements for the two protocols:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/\/ A position in an x-y coordinate system.","struct Position: Equatable, Hashable {","    var x: Int","    var y: Int","","    init(_ x: Int, _ y: Int) {","        self.x = x","        self.y = y","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance, you can use the equal-to operator ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":") or the not-equal-to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operator ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"!="},{"type":"text","text":") with any two instances of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let availablePositions = [Position(0, 0), Position(0, 1), Position(1, 0)]","let gemPosition = Position(1, 0)","","for position in availablePositions {","    if gemPosition == position {","        print(\"Gem found at (\\(position.x), \\(position.y))!\")","    } else {","        print(\"No gem at (\\(position.x), \\(position.y))\")","    }","}","\/\/ No gem at (0, 0)","\/\/ No gem at (0, 1)","\/\/ Gem found at (1, 0)!",""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance means that you can store positions in a set and quickly check"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether you’ve visited a position before, as shown in the following example:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var visitedPositions: Set = [Position(0, 0), Position(1, 0)]","let currentPosition = Position(1, 3)","","if visitedPositions.contains(currentPosition) {","    print(\"Already visited (\\(currentPosition.x), \\(currentPosition.y))\")","} else {","    print(\"First time at (\\(currentPosition.x), \\(currentPosition.y))\")","    visitedPositions.insert(currentPosition)","}","\/\/ First time at (1, 3)",""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In addition to simplifying your code, this automatic conformance reduces errors,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because any new properties you add to your custom types are automatically included"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when hashing and testing for equality. A type is eligible for automatic conformance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" when it’s a structure or an enumeration that meets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"these criteria:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a structure, "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" its stored properties must conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For an enumeration, "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"all"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" its associated values must conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":". (Enumerations without associated values have "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conformance even without declaring adoption.)"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Conform-Manually-to-Equatable-and-Hashable","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Conform Manually to Equatable and Hashable"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You need to manually implement "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance for a type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in these cases:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The type doesn’t meet the criteria listed in the previous section."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You want to customize the type’s conformance."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You want to extend a type declared in another file or module to conform."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"code":["class Player {","    var name: String","    var position: Position","","    init(name: String, position: Position) {","        self.name = name","        self.position = position","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Player"},{"type":"text","text":" type is a class, so it doesn’t qualify for automatic synthesis of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" requirements. To make this class conform to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol, declare conformance in an extension and implement the  static "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":" operator"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method. Compare each significant property for equality in your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":" method’s implementation:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension Player: Equatable {","    static func ==(lhs: Player, rhs: Player) -> Bool {","        return lhs.name == rhs.name && lhs.position == rhs.position","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To make "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Player"},{"type":"text","text":" conform to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol, declare conformance in another"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"extension and implement the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hash(into:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method. In the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hash(into:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method, call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"combine(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method on the provided hasher with each significant property:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension Player: Hashable {","    func hash(into hasher: inout Hasher) {","        hasher.combine(name)","        hasher.combine(position)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Use-All-Significant-Properties-for-Equatable-and-Hashable","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Use All Significant Properties for Equatable and Hashable"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When implementing the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":" method and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hash(into:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method, use all the properties"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that affect whether two instances of your custom type are considered equal. In the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implementations above, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Player"},{"type":"text","text":" type uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"position"},{"type":"text","text":" in both methods."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If your type contains properties that don’t affect whether two instances are considered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equal, exclude those properties from comparison in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":" method and from hashing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hash(into:)"},{"type":"text","text":". For example, a type might cache an expensive computed value so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that it only needs to calculate it once. If you compare two instances of that type,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not the computed value has been cached shouldn’t affect their equality,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the cached value should be excluded from comparison and hashing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Always use the same properties in both your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hash(into:)"},{"type":"text","text":" methods."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Using different groups of properties in the two methods can lead to unexpected behavior"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or performance when using your custom type in sets and dictionaries."}]}],"name":"Important","type":"aside"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/adopting-common-protocols"]}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Adopting Common Protocols"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Make your custom types easier to use by ensuring that they conform to Swift protocols."}],"references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Hashable":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Hashable"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Hashable","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/hashable","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that can be hashed into a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hasher"},{"type":"text","text":" to produce an integer hash value."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Hashable","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Hashable"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swift","role":"collection","title":"Swift","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","abstract":[{"text":"Build apps using a powerful open language.","type":"text"}]},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/Equatable":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that can be compared for value equality."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Equatable"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/equatable","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Equatable","title":"Equatable","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Equatable"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/choosing-between-structures-and-classes":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/choosing-between-structures-and-classes","type":"topic","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/choosing-between-structures-and-classes","kind":"article","title":"Choosing Between Structures and Classes","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Decide how to store data and model behavior."}]}}}